.TH BC250\-WCM 1 "2026-10-18" "bc250-wcm 0.2.0" "User Manual"
.SH NAME
bc250\-wcm \- Wireless Controller Monitor: Bluetooth pads and USB 2.4 GHz receivers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bc250\-wcm
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B bc250\-wcm hid
.RB { list | descriptor | capture | analyze }
.RI ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bc250\-wcm
(Wireless Controller Monitor, formerly bc250\-btmon) shows game controllers
connected over Bluetooth and through dedicated USB 2.4 GHz receivers, and
monitors one to four of them at a time, of either kind, in a terminal dashboard in the style of
.BR btop (1):
the RSSI of the live link with a history graph, minimum, maximum, average and
standard deviation, disconnects, reconnects and down time, battery, and the
device's events.
.PP
Adapters, devices and their state come from BlueZ over the system D\-Bus. The
RSSI of a live link comes from the kernel Management API (Get Connection
Information, the command behind
.BR "btmgmt conn\-info" );
it needs CAP_NET_ADMIN, which a small read\-only helper started through
.BR sudo (8)
provides \(em the interface itself stays unprivileged. Kernel Bluetooth
messages (HCI command timeouts, USB resets, firmware) are followed through
.BR journalctl (1).
.PP
Adapters are identified by their controller address (plus the USB port when
two adapters share one), not by their
.I hciN
index. When an adapter resets and re\-registers under another index, monitoring
resumes on its own and the event log records the remap.
.PP
A disconnect is recorded as a gap, never as an RSSI of 0. The program shows no
packet loss, latency or "link quality" figures; the colour bands are thresholds
from the configuration and are marked as an approximation. On BR/EDR links the
value is relative to the controller's golden receive range (dB), not dBm.
.PP
The program never resets an adapter, restarts a service or starts discovery by
itself.
.PP
USB controllers and receivers are found in sysfs, without privileges, and
identified by their place on the bus, so a receiver that switches its product
ID (8BitDo Ultimate 2C: 2dc8:301c idle, 2dc8:310a with a pad linked) or is
re\-plugged stays the same device. A receiver reports no signal strength and,
with stock firmware, no battery: both are shown as n/a, never estimated.
Instead the panel shows the link state taken from the product ID and the pad's
input activity (events per second from its evdev node, read\-only, never
grabbed) \(em a measure of use, not of the radio.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interval " \fISEC\fR"
Sampling interval, default 1.0 (0.2\(en60). Changed at runtime with
.B +
and
.BR \- .
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-monitor " \fIMAC\fR ..."
Start monitoring these one to four devices right away.
.TP
.B \-\-list
Print adapters and devices and exit. Needs no privileges.
.TP
.B \-\-json
The same as JSON.
.TP
.BI \-\-headless " SEC"
No interface: sample the devices given with
.B \-\-monitor
for
.I SEC
seconds, print one line per sample and a summary.
.TP
.BI \-\-export " FILE"
After
.BR \-\-headless ,
write the measurements to
.I FILE
(CSV, or JSON when the name ends in .json).
.TP
.BI \-\-record " FILE.csv"
Append every sample to a CSV file as it is taken.
.TP
.BR \-\-rssi\-backend " auto|helper|direct|btmgmt|none"
Where link RSSI comes from. auto: the installed helper without a prompt, else
the bundled helper after one
.BR "sudo \-v" ,
else none; as root, the mgmt socket directly.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-sudo
Never ask for a password.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-kernel\-log
Do not follow the kernel log.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-usb
Skip USB controllers and receivers.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-input\-activity
Do not count input events.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " FILE"
Configuration file instead of
.IR ~/.config/bc250\-wcm/config.ini .
.TP
.B \-\-print\-config
Print an example configuration with every setting and its default.
.TP
.B \-\-ascii
ASCII characters only.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
No colours (also when NO_COLOR is set).
.TP
.B \-\-demo
A simulation: two pads, a disconnect, an HCI timeout and an hci0 \(-> hci1
re\-registration. No hardware needed.
.TP
.BI \-\-demo\-speed " N"
Speed up the simulation timeline N times (with
.BR \-\-demo ).
.TP
.BR \-\-lang " pl|en"
Interface language.
.SH HID RESEARCH
.B bc250\-wcm hid
inspects HID interfaces, vendor\-defined ones above all, strictly read\-only:
nodes are opened read\-only and no code sends a report. A node is selected as
.IR hidrawN ,
.IR /dev/hidrawN ,
or \(em stable across re\-plugging \(em
.IR vid:pid:interface ,
e.g. 2dc8:310a:2.
.TP
.BR "hid list " [ \-\-json ]
Every hidraw node: selector, name, usage pages, reports, access.
.TP
.BI "hid descriptor " SEL
The report descriptor, raw and decoded.
.TP
.BI "hid capture " SEL " \fR[\fB\-t\fR \fISEC\fR] [\fB\-o\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-\-marks\fR] [\fB\-\-quiet\fR]"
Print input reports as hex (changed bytes in brackets) and save them as JSON
lines. With \-\-marks every line typed on stdin becomes a labelled timestamp;
\-\-quiet only saves.
.TP
.BI "hid analyze " "FILE \fR[\fIFILE2\fR] [\fB\-\-window\fR \fISEC\fR]"
Constant and changing bytes per report ID, value ranges, differences between
two captures, bytes that changed within SEC seconds (default 1) after each mark.
.SH KEYS
.SS Device picker
.TP
.BR Space ", " 1 \(en 9
Select or deselect a device (up to four).
.TP
.B Enter
Monitor the selection.
.TP
.BR / ", " f ", " o
Search, cycle the filter (all, connected, paired, discovered), cycle the sort order.
.TP
.B d
Start or stop discovery on the adapter. LE scanning is what timed out
(opcode 0x2042) on RTL8761BU dongles; leave it off next to connected pads.
.SS Dashboard
.TP
.BR Tab ", arrows, " 1 \(en 4
Choose a panel.
.TP
.B Enter
Device details.
.TP
.B s
Change the selection; history is kept.
.TP
.BR p ", " l ", " r
Pause sampling, event log, reset statistics.
.TP
.BR e ", " j
Export CSV, export JSON.
.TP
.BR c ", " g
Compact panels, Braille or ASCII graph.
.SS Everywhere
.TP
.BR h ", " ? ", " Esc ", " q
Help, back, quit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/bc250\-wcm/config.ini
Configuration (INI). See
.BR \-\-print\-config .
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/bc250\-wcm/events.jsonl
The event log, one JSON object per line; rotated at 2 MiB.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/bc250\-wcm/selection
The devices monitored last time, preselected on the next start.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/bc250\-wcm/receivers
USB places seen as an idle receiver, so a later 2dc8:310a there is known to be
the receiver and not the pad on a cable.
.TP
.I /etc/udev/rules.d/70\-bc250\-wcm.rules
Optional uaccess rule for the receiver's hidraw nodes (install.sh \-\-udev).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/bc250\-wcm/exports/
Exports.
.TP
.I /usr/local/libexec/bc250\-wcm/rssi\-helper
The helper installed by
.BR "install.sh \-\-rssi\-helper" ,
together with
.IR /etc/sudoers.d/bc250\-wcm .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BC250_LANG
Interface language, pl or en.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disables colours.
.TP
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME ", " XDG_STATE_HOME ", " XDG_DATA_HOME
Base directories of the files above.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B bc250\-wcm \-\-list
What is there.
.TP
.B bc250\-wcm \-m E4:17:D8:00:00:01 E4:17:D8:00:00:02
Two pads, straight to the dashboard.
.TP
.B bc250\-wcm \-\-headless 120 \-m E4:17:D8:00:00:01 \-\-export run.json
Two minutes of samples to a file, no interface.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 when
.B \-\-list
or
.B \-\-json
could not reach BlueZ, or
.B \-\-headless
found none of the devices; 2 for invalid arguments or no terminal.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR btmgmt (1),
.BR bluetoothctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1),
.BR bc250\-mon (1)
.PP
docs/architecture.md, docs/permissions.md, docs/usb\-receivers.md and
docs/hardware\-testing.md in the tool's directory.
